course: dictionary
lesson: 14239
title: Nearness and closeness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nearness is a noun. It means being near, or close to something or someone. Near is the describing word, and -ness turns it into a noun, so nearness is the state of being near. «The nearness of the sea meant we could hear the waves all night.» Here nearness is about distance: the sea was close.
explain: Nearness can also be about time. «The nearness of the exams made Priya study every night.» The exams were coming soon, so nearness means being close in time. Ask yourself: is the thing close in space, in time, or between people?
explain: Nearness can show how close people feel. «Ben felt a warm nearness to his best friend, even when they were apart.» Ben did not measure a distance here. He felt close to his friend, so nearness means closeness in feeling. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: Nearness means being close.
fact: Nearness can be about distance, time, or how close people feel.
fact: Nearness is uncountable, so we usually say «the nearness» rather than «a nearness».
fact: The root word is near, and adding -ness changes it into a noun.
fact: Closeness is a similar word that can often replace nearness, as in «the closeness of the sea».
exercise: «The nearness of the sea meant we could hear the waves all night.» What does nearness mean here? | Being far away in time | *Being close in distance | Being close in a friendship | Being very loud
exercise: «The nearness of the exams made Priya study every night.» What does nearness mean here? | *Being close in time | Being far away in space | Being very quiet | Being close in a friendship
exercise: «Ben felt a warm nearness to his best friend, even when they were apart.» What kind of closeness is this? | Closeness in time | *Closeness in feeling | Closeness in size | Closeness in distance
test: «The nearness of the holidays made the whole class cheer.» What does nearness mean here? | *Being close in time | Being close in distance | Being close in a friendship | Being far from home
test: Which word means nearly the same as nearness in «the nearness of the shops»? | Remoteness | Tallness | Darkness | *Closeness
exam: «The nearness of her grandmother made Kiara feel safe, even in a crowded room.» What does nearness mean here? | Being loud and busy | *Being close in feeling | Being far away in distance | Being close in time
